From fb01d9635b3152add1427d355ee24f2456dc5397 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:41:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0207 -- MIDI timing off the render rate: plan
 ahead on the main loop, play from the SB IRQ

WHY: the 8.3 re-run on HW-486-66 (PLAN.md, SB4O/SB4W, 2026-09-23): the 640x480 intro renders at
~6 fps, the fixed-timestep loop runs its catch-up ticks back to back, and MidiPoll -> midi_sched_tick
dispatched every event due since the last render in one batch: 465 of 483 lateness records were
regular 150-200 ms gaps, 72% of events more than 50 ms late -- the operator heard "music speeds up
randomly". The scheduler and sinks (hub shared code, FPU + unlocked state) cannot run in an ISR.

WHAT: with SDL patch 0193, the player keeps running the same scheduler and sinks on the main loop but
AHEAD of time. At song start (MidiInit, and MidiPlay after a stop) MidiIsrBegin() takes the ISR replay
when the backend maps to a capture kind (OPL3 -> 1, WaveBlaster -> 2), the SB IRQ has fired at least
once, no other MIDI player owns the replay, SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable() accepts (SB open; for WB only the
blind direct transport) and DOSAGS_MIDI_TICK is not "poll"; otherwise the main-loop poll stays, as
before. In isr mode each MidiPoll plans from the last planned slot (never earlier than two IRQs out: an entry
stamped for the very next IRQ can miss it if that IRQ fires while the plan is being written) to now + lookahead (default 2 s,
DOSAGS_MIDI_LOOKAHEAD_MS), one IRQ period (512 frames, 46.44 ms at 11025 Hz) at a time: set the
stamp to that slot's IRQ index, midi_sched_tick() to that slot's song time; the sink's port writes
are captured and the SB ISR writes them out at that IRQ, whatever the main loop is doing. Song time is
plan time minus skipped gaps: if the plan ever falls behind the device (a stall longer than the
lookahead, or a resume from pause) the gap is skipped in song time rather than replayed late in one
burst, and counted (plan_behind; not after a resume). Stop and destruction drop the planned-ahead
writes, queue the sink's note-offs for the next IRQ, then disable the replay (which writes out what
is left at once) so the next song's chip detection is direct. Pause stops planning; up to the
lookahead already queued still plays, then notes hold, as the poll's pause did.

Status: "DosMidiBackend: MIDI tick isr|poll" at song start; the MIDI fragment gains midi_tick=isr|poll.
In isr mode it reports period_us, lookahead, isr_writes, late_writes (written >= 1 IRQ after their
stamp), late_max_ms, isr_burst (most writes in one IRQ), qfull, qsync / qdropped (entries a disable wrote
out / discarded), plan_behind and clk (device-clock
song ms against the RTC); in poll mode the 0206 fields as before. The mixer's MIDI fragment buffer
grows 192 -> 320 bytes and the status buffers 384 -> 512 (the isr fragment is ~260 characters; a
first build truncated it at clk=).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
